-- title:
--   Level automorphisms transport node place-sets and Igusa ends
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ its residue field is written $\kappa$. The ambient function fields are $F_1 =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (itself generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the series $q$-expanded from $j_q$ at the divisors of $M'$), and $F =$ `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change of the function field of the $H$-level curve of level $q^2M'$, where $H =$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Places `Place K F` are valuation subrings of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$, whose ideals are principal; `evalAt` is the constant in $K$ representing the residue of an element of the valuation subring (and $0$ off it), and `ord` is the associated normalised order.
--
--   Base data. A prime $q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`), a finite set $W$ of places of $C =$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ` (`hW`), that is, the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at the generator `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`; an inclusion $F_1 \le F$ (`hle`); a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from $F_1$ to $C$ (a valuation subring of $F_1$ tracing $A$ on constants, a surjective residue map onto $C$ with kernel the maximal ideal, and a place map preserving degrees and orders), subject to `hR₀`: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $F_1$, that image lies in the integers of $R_0$ and its $R_0$-residue, viewed as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally a distinguished member $s \in W$.
--
--   Constant-field block. An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$; writing $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ for the contraction of $A$ to $k_0$, the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` state that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is Henselian local, and has algebraically closed residue field; `hκ` states that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   Auxiliary primes and uniformisers. A prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Also $\pi_t \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\pi_t^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi_t \in A$.
--
--   Layer block. A type $\iota$, a family $K$ of intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$, each finite over $k_0$ (`hKfin`), valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ whose membership agrees with that of $A$ (`hAn`), an index $n_0$ with $K_{n_0} \le K_n$ for all $n$, and cofinality `hKcof`: every finite subset of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is contained in the image of some $K_n$. Tameness `htame`: every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ with `A.tameCharacter πt τ = 1` fixes $K_{n_0}$ pointwise.
--
--   Bottom layer. An intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ whose membership agrees with that of $A$ (`hAb`), and a generator $\varpi_b \ne 0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   Assertion. With $F$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the following holds for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ satisfying the four conditions: (i) $f \in F_0$ exactly when all Laurent coefficients of $f$ lie in $k_0$; (ii) the subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with $F_0$ is all of $F$; (iii) $F_0$ is stable under every level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; (iv) linear disjointness from the constants: for each finite extension $K'/k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, each $m$, each $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and each family $a_i$ in the compositum of $K'$ and $F_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$.
--
--   For such an $F_0$, for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$, every subring $B$ of $F$ with an $A_b$-algebra structure `alg`, the hypotheses `hjR` (the image $j$ of $j_q$ in $F_1$ lies in the integers of $R_0$), `hjs` (its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$), `hJK` (`jqNModC` of level $q$ lies in $F$), an element $a_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with `hpin`: the residue of $a_0$ raised to the $q$-th power equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $j$, and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$, the following implication holds.
--
--   The antecedent is a conjunction of the following groups. (1) Constants and uniformiser for $W_0$: an element of $k_0$ lies in $A$ iff its image lies in $W_0$; $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal. (2) Specialisation at $s$: for every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change lies in the integers of $R_0$, if $g$ has non-negative order at every place of $F_1$ at which $j$ has non-negative order, and if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose $A$-residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $g$ and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$. (3) Level invariance of $W_0$: for $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $f \in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` again in $F_0$, membership of $f$ in $W_0$ is equivalent to membership of its image. (4) The model $B$ over $A_b$: the structure map $A_b \to B$ is the inclusion into $F$; $B$ is contained in the compositum of $K_b$ and $F_0$, and every element of that compositum is a ratio of elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; $B/(\varpi_b)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime; an element of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ exactly when it is a ratio $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $\varpi_b \nmid h$; $j \in B$; $B$ is stable under the level automorphisms for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; there is $b \in B \cap F_0$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ that agrees with $A$ on constants, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$, and for which $p(j)$ is a unit of $V$ for every monic polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$; and for each $s' \in W$ with $s' \ne s$ there is such a $b \in B \cap F_0$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ that agrees with $A$ on constants and satisfies the specialisation condition (2) with $s'$ and $V$ in place of $s$ and $W_0$. (5) Drinfeld identification of the special fibre: for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ and every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and for each $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ C_s`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field of the $C_s$-part of the $H$-action on the Drinfeld function field) with: $|C_s| = 2\,$`placeWidthChar q M' s`; kernel of $\rho$ the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ on $A_b$ given by reduction to $\kappa$ followed by the structure map; every element of the target a ratio $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$; the image of $\rho$ consisting exactly of the elements coming from `CoordRing q κ` inside the Drinfeld function field; and $\rho$ intertwining `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` with [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1) \in$ `hSubgroup q`. (6) The node block: `nodes` has $q+1$ elements; there is a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$ generated by the constants lying in $A$ together with a finite set, contained in every $O \in$ `nodes`, each such $O$ being the localisation of $B_c$ at its own units; the level automorphisms permute `nodes`, and for each $\zeta$ they act transitively on `nodes`; distinct nodes $O \ne O'$ are separated by an element of both which is a non-unit in $O$ and a unit in $O'$; every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ agreeing with $A$ on constants and satisfying the specialisation condition (2) at $s$ either contains all of $B$ or dominates some node $O$ (that is, $O \subseteq V$ and the non-units of $O$ lie in the maximal ideal of $V$). (7) Per-node crossing data: every $O \in$ `nodes` is contained in $W_0$, is local and Noetherian, agrees with $A$ on constants, and has each of its elements congruent modulo non-units to a constant from $k_0 \cap A$; moreover there are $E_0 \ge 1$ together with a unit $v$ of $A \cap k_0$ such that $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{2w}v$ with $w =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with `UVCrossingModel` of the adic completion of $A_0$ at the parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$ (that is, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring by $X_0X_1 - \pi_0^{E_0}$), and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that model, such that $c_xc_y = \pi_0^{E_0}u$, $\iota$ carries constants to `const`, $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U\,U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V\,V$, $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ while $c_x$ does not, the germ $\mathrm{jqNModC} - a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$ with $\iota$ of it equal to a unit times $V^e$ for some $e \ge 1$; there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, agreeing with $A$ on constants, a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, possessing an element $t$ such that any polynomial over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$ whose value at $t$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ has all its coefficients in that maximal ideal, with $c_x$ in and $c_y$ off the maximal ideal of $W_x$, such that every $g$ as in (2) (with the order condition relative to $j$, but without any condition at $s$) has its image in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ precisely when its $R_0$-residue vanishes, and, when that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, lies in $O$ and differs from every matching constant by a non-unit of $O$; and each node $O' \ne O$ has an element outside $W_x$. Finally there is a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ contained in $B \cap O$, all of whose elements have non-negative order at every place of $F$ where $j$ does, with $O$ the localisation of $B_x$ at its units, every element of $F_0$ a ratio of elements of $B_x$ with nonzero denominator, $B_x$ generated by the constants lying in $A$ together with a finite set, and containing an element $b$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ that agrees with $A$ on constants, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$ with $p(j)$ a unit for all monic $p$ over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$, and fails to contain some element of $O$.
--
--   Given this antecedent, the conclusion is the following. Let $F_{SS}$ be a field that is an algebra over $\kappa$ and $R$ a regular prolongation of $A$ from $F$ to $F_{SS}$ (a valuation subring of $F$ tracing $A$ on constants, with surjective residue map onto $F_{SS}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, and such that every nonzero element of $F$ can be scaled by a constant into the integers with nonzero residue), and suppose $R$ traces $W_0$: an element of $F_0$ lies in the integers of $R$ exactly when it lies in $W_0$. Let $N$ be a finite set of places of $F_{SS}$ over $\kappa$ and `Oof` a map from places to subrings of $F_0$ carrying $N$ into `nodes`, onto `nodes`, and injectively on $N$. Let $S$ assign to each place of $F_{SS}$ a set of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ so that for $nd \in N$ a place $P$ belongs to $S(nd)$ exactly when $P$ dominates `Oof nd`, that is, all of `Oof nd` lies in the valuation subring of $P$ and for every non-unit $f$ of `Oof nd` the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$. Suppose each $nd \in N$ is the centre of `Oof nd` for $R$: the $R$-residue of every element of `Oof nd` in the integers of $R$ lies in the valuation subring of $nd$, non-units of `Oof nd` having residue in the maximal ideal of $nd$, and any place $y$ of $F_{SS}$ with these two properties equals $nd$. Let $FIx$ be a family of fields over $\kappa$ indexed by the places of $F_{SS}$, $Rx$ a family of regular prolongations of $A$ from $F$ to $FIx$, and $Wx$ a family of valuation subrings of $F_0$, such that for $nd \in N$: $Rx(nd)$ traces $Wx(nd)$ on $F_0$; `Oof nd` is contained in $Wx(nd)$; $\pi_0$ lies in the maximal ideal of $Wx(nd)$; and there is $c_{yO} \in$ `Oof nd` that is a unit of $Wx(nd)$, whose $R$-residue is $0$, and for which $Wx(nd)$ is minimal, in the sense that every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ containing `Oof nd`, having $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal and $c_{yO}$ as a unit, contains $Wx(nd)$.
--
--   Then both of the following hold. First, for every $\zeta' \in$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ there is a map $\tau_N$ on the places of $F_{SS}$ over $\kappa$ such that for each $nd \in N$: $\tau_N(nd) \in N$; for every place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the translate of $P$ by `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` lies in $S(nd)$ exactly when $P$ lies in $S(\tau_N(nd))$; and the pullback of the integers of $Rx(nd)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` equals the integers of $Rx(\tau_N(nd))$. Second, for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphism group of $F$ generated by the level automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and for every witness that $\tau$ preserves the integers of $R$, each $nd \in N$ satisfies: the translate of $nd$ by the induced automorphism `R.resAut τ` of $F_{SS}$ over $\kappa$ again lies in $N$, and [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.smulDisc τ (S nd)`](def/AlgebraicCurve_ResidueDiscs.html#L120), the set of places $P$ with $\tau^{-1}\cdot P \in S(nd)$, equals $S$ of that translate.
--
--   This is the equivariance step for the node data of the semistable fibre at $q$ of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ with units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$: the $\Gamma_0(M')$-level automorphisms permute the $q+1$ nodes of the supersingular fibre over the place $s$, together with the place-sets dominating them and the Igusa-side prolongations attached to them, and the induced residue automorphisms move the node places of $F_{SS}$ and their discs accordingly. It is used in the construction of the per-node charts and Hasse germs at a node centre, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
